# Simulated alignments — ~750 MB, and reproducible. Regenerate with
# shell/generate_alignments.sh (needs wgsim, pbsim, minimap2, samtools), then
# shell/load_alignments.sh to wire them into every build under builds/.
# The small tracked inputs that sit alongside them in data/ — hg19mod.fa(.fai),
# hg19_17.chrom.sizes, R103.model — are not matched by these patterns.
data/*.bam
data/*.bam.bai
data/*.cram
data/*.cram.crai
data/*.bw

# Multi-sample VCFs for the ecosystem VCF benchmark, ~37 MB. Regenerate with
# shell/generate_variants.sh, which needs nothing but node — the records come
# from a seeded RNG, so every machine gets byte-identical files.
data/variants.*.vcf

# jbrowse-web builds under test. Each is a deployed build plus symlinked copies
# of the alignment data; stage them per README ("Builds compared").
builds/

node_modules/

# V8 CPU profiles from flameprofile.ts / interaction-profile.ts, ~600 KB each.
# The conclusions drawn from them are in flame/*.md, which are tracked.
*.cpuprofile

# Puppeteer verify/probe output
screenshots/

# Top-level logs from building and generating; results/*.log is tracked, since
# those are the raw per-run numbers behind the tables.
/build_webgl.log
/gen_alignments.log

# Derived flamegraph intermediates (from *.cpuprofile, which is ignored)
flame/*.folded
flame/*.svg

# The eight library versions ecosystem/ compares: each is a clone of a GMOD repo
# at a tag pinned in ecosystem/versions.json, carrying its own .git and its own
# node_modules. ecosystem/setup.sh rebuilds them in a few minutes.
ecosystem/.libs/
